In article <2326@trlluna.trl.oz> soh@shiva.trl.oz (kam hung soh) writes:
>I don't know whether this is a quirk, but to see a mimic in a shop, I
>merely walk in one step, and back out again.  I can still see
>(remember?) all the items in the shop, except for creatures (mimics
>included) and the shopkeeper.

My understanding of mimics in the shop is that when you leave the shop
the objects will still be on the screen, until a creature, such as a pet
or monster or the shopkeeper walks across that space, and then it will
show up as a regular space.  The second part is that the monsters,(mimics,
hobbits, pets, shopkeepers, etc.) will not be seen when outside the shop.
Please note this information is based upon my playing experience not by
looking at the source codes.
